“Rodina-Haskovo” AD is a leader in the manufacture of machines and equipment for the food and wine industry in Bulgaria and Europe. Currently the LB company is suffering by using old and uneffective methods of heating its production premises. This is affecting the employees and the production capacity. The idea is to create a comfortable working environment in the old production hall, for which it will be built radiant (panel) heating on natural gas. This heating is highly efficient and without emission of harmful emissions. At the moment the heating is done with local wood stoves, which is not effective and smokes the room.Though the project, the company will implement at its premises a new panel heating and concrete construction, improving the working conditions in order to be suitable for all year round activities, which will significantly increase the production capacity. The PB - Gerontidia A. & Co. will set up a 500 KW photovoltaic station in Neochori, Orestiada. The shareholders of the company have already begun the licensing procedures and they have already received two basic licenses. The investment plan aims at:

1. Introducing a new service of the two enterprises by incorporating new technology;
2. improving service quality for both enterprises by increasing the technological content of the service;
3. reducing service and production costs;
4. Introduction of efficient marketing systems through the planned joint certification of quality management systems and joint marketing plans of the partners.

Since the beginning of the implementation of the EU Strategy for the Danube Region in June 2011, Slovenian and Serbian partners have been working together to manage and facilitate the coordination of the Priority Area 1b: "To improve mobility and multimodality – rail, road and air links".
The project encourages both PACs in their efforts to continue stable, effective, inclusive and innovative implementation of this Priority Area, which improves the cooperation between all participating countries and regions represented in the Steering Group.

Also in the next six years, all efforts will be made to achieve the continuation of main objectives already identified in the past by EUSDR PA1b. In particular it will:
- support SG work through the organisation of Steering Group meetings and regular contacts with SG members by (mobile) phone or/and e-mail;
- keep strong links with EUSDR governance structures (EUSDR Governance bodies, DG REGIO, NCs, DSP) and DTP;
- support exchange of experience and best practices with all relevant actors of the PA through the organisation of stakeholder conferences and other stakeholder events (seminars, workshops). The aim of these events is to gather the stakeholders of the Priority Area to follow up the ongoing implementation, discuss current issues, solve bottlenecks of the implementation and develop new project ideas;
- contribute to alignment of regional and national transport policies with the EU transport policy by cooperation with the European Commission (DG REGIO, DG MOVE and DG NEAR);
- facilitate and support ongoing and planned projects, as well as project initiatives or ideas relevant for the Danube region. 

If needed the work might be modified in order to be aligned with new, upcoming EU policies and in particular the EU transport policy.

Inland waterway transport still has unexploited capacities compared to other transport modes – in Europe and even more so in the Danube region – due to various challenges, such as navigational bottlenecks, a partly outdated inland fleet and a shortage of qualified personnel. These macro-regional challenges require the mobilization of resources and close coordination of activities among all Danube region countries. This project is therefore aimed at establishing a stable and effective governance system for PA1a, aiming to increase the share of environmentally friendly inland waterway transport in the total transport of freight across the Danube region, in accordance with the EUSDR Action Plan. PA1a will focus on the implementation of individual work programmes for each of the six PA1a working groups, aligned with the six thematic actions of the EUSDR Action Plan.

The core achievements of this project will include:


1. An effective governance structure within PA1a, in particular with regard to the intensive involvement of the PA1a Steering Group members in the implementation of the EUSDR Action Plan; 


2. The support to policy development and policy initiatives in the field of inland navigation;


3. Enhanced coordination between core stakeholders, both within PA1a (in particular the six thematic PA1a Working Groups) and with further stakeholders from the EUSDR (other PAs/DSP), EU institutions and further stakeholders in and outside the Danube region; 


4. The support to strategic projects, project development and capitalisation of project outcomes.

